I"]<p>ContentGen is an open-source tool that generates programming questions for data science courses using large language models (LLMs). We iteratively improved the tool through prompt engineering and evaluated its effectiveness using a test set of 91 questions and custom metrics for correctness, contextual fit, and coherence. Our study shows that structured prompts with instructional summaries significantly improve output quality. A usability study with instructors further confirms the tool’s usefulness. This project offers a practical approach for improving LLM-generated educational content.</p>
